.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt IRQ_WAIT 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm irq_wait
.Nd wait for device interrupts
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Fn irq_wait irq timeout_ns
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm blocks until the interrupt has fired at least once since the last
.Nm
or
.Xr irq_ack 2
and returns the number of accumulated firings (at least 1).
A
.Fa timeout_ns
of zero waits forever; otherwise an elapsed timeout returns 0.
.Pp
A level-triggered
.Dv LEGACY
line is masked after delivery until
.Xr irq_ack 2 ,
so a device that keeps its line asserted cannot storm the CPU.
MSI/MSI-X are edge-triggered and need no re-arm, but
.Xr irq_ack 2
is still the driver's quiesce barrier before the handle is closed.
.Pp
If another thread closes the last handle while
.Nm
is blocked, every waiter is woken; the one whose handle is gone returns
.Er EIO .
The
.Em Irq
object stays alive until the waiter returns, and the wait-queue entry is
removed, so no stale waiter is left behind.
.Pp
The
.Em Irq
handle can also be registered in an event queue with
.Xr evq_ctl 2
and the
.Dv SIGNALED
event; the pending counter is then reported as readiness until an
.Nm
consumes it.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EBADF
.Fa irq
is not an interrupt handle.
.It Er EACCES
The handle lacks the
.Dv READ
right.
.It Er EIO
The handle was closed while the thread was blocked in
.Nm .
.El
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
